{
 "dur": 74.4,
 "vo": [
  {
   "id": "v01",
   "t": 0.4,
   "chunks": [
    "Why does the air from a vent",
    "hug the ceiling?",
    "Let's follow it",
    "from the blower."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02",
   "t": 5.21,
   "chunks": [
    "A spinning blower wheel",
    "flings air outward,",
    "building a pressure difference",
    "of about half an inch of water.",
    "Tiny, but enough",
    "to push air through the house."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03",
   "t": 14.51,
   "chunks": [
    "In the main duct, air moves",
    "about 900 feet per minute.",
    "Where the duct narrows,",
    "it speeds up.",
    "Where it widens, it slows,",
    "and pressure climbs back."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v04",
   "t": 24.26,
   "chunks": [
    "Friction, and every elbow,",
    "costs pressure.",
    "Branch ducts run slower,",
    "about 600 feet per minute."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v05",
   "t": 30.76,
   "chunks": [
    "At the diffuser,",
    "angled vanes fling the stream",
    "sideways, along the ceiling."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v06",
   "t": 35.71,
   "chunks": [
    "The fast jet drags air",
    "out of the gap above it.",
    "Pressure drops there,",
    "and the jet gets pulled",
    "onto the ceiling.",
    "That's the Coanda effect."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v07",
   "t": 44.32,
   "chunks": [
    "Then it breaks into",
    "turbulent eddies,",
    "mixing and slowing.",
    "Engineers size it to drop",
    "below 50 feet per minute",
    "by the end of its throw."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v08",
   "t": 52.97,
   "chunks": [
    "By the time it reaches you,",
    "it's a gentle draft,",
    "under 40 feet per minute.",
    "Warm air rises,",
    "cool air sinks."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v09",
   "t": 60.44,
   "chunks": [
    "That's why it hugs the ceiling:",
    "a fast jet,",
    "a low-pressure gap,",
    "and a surface to cling to."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v10",
   "t": 66.73,
   "chunks": [
    "What should we",
    "take apart next?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v11",
   "t": 68.93,
   "chunks": [
    "Congrats! You've discovered",
    "how air flows through a vent."
   ]
  }
 ]
}